---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageBanner from '../../components/PageBanner.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Sanshi Bio';
const description = 'How Sanshi Bio handles personal information and pigeon sample data: collection, purposes, third parties, retention, transfers and rights.';

const breadcrumbLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://sanshibio.net/en/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy Policy' },
  ],
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={[breadcrumbLd]}>
  <PageBanner title="Privacy Policy" description="How we handle personal information, samples and test data" breadcrumb="Privacy Policy" />

  <section class="container-site py-16">
    <div class="prose-sanshi mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500"><em>Last updated: 2026-11-24</em></p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">1. Scope and controller</h2>
      <p>
        This policy applies to sanshibio.net and its English pages, operated by Hebei Sanshi
        Biotechnology Co., Ltd. (“Sanshi Bio”). We process personal information and sample information
        for racing-pigeon gene testing, pathogen testing, paternity testing, sex identification and
        related services. It does not cover the independent processing of third-party websites,
        payment platforms, carriers or social-media services.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">2. Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Contact and order details:</b> name, phone, email, WeChat/WhatsApp, address, company or loft name.</li>
        <li><b>Bird and sample details:</b> bird ID, ring number, breed/bloodline information, sample type, collection date and test requested.</li>
        <li><b>Transaction and communication records:</b> quotation, order status, payment status, invoice/receipt information and support messages.</li>
        <li><b>Technical and access data:</b> IP address, browser type, pages requested, timestamps and necessary security logs.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We collect only what is necessary to test, report, communicate, provide support and meet legal
        obligations. Do not send sensitive personal information unrelated to the test in an enquiry.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">3. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
      <p>
        We use information to perform tests and issue reports, receive and re-test samples, prepare
        quotations and fulfil orders, provide support and handle complaints, keep quality records,
        maintain security and prevent fraud, and comply with applicable law. Depending on your
        jurisdiction and the context, the legal basis may be performance of a contract, consent,
        compliance with a legal obligation, or our legitimate business interests.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">4. Samples and test data</h2>
      <p>
        Samples and test data are used to perform the commissioned project, support necessary
        re-testing, maintain quality control and communicate about the service. A sample may contain a
        bird's genetic information; we handle it for the test and do not use it for unrelated purposes.
        Retention, destruction and re-test use follow the
        <a href="/en/service-policy">Testing Service Policy</a>, the order and applicable law.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reports are normally issued to the commissioning client or a written authorised recipient. We
        do not disclose reports or individual results to unrelated third parties except where required
        by law or necessary to protect a vital interest.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">5. Service providers</h2>
      <p>
        We may use service providers in these categories: laboratories/testing partners, sample
        couriers and logistics, payment/banking, cloud hosting and email, IT support and professional
        advisers. They receive information only as needed for the service and are required to protect
        it under contract and applicable law. Links to third-party websites are governed by those
        parties' own policies.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">6. Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain information only for the period needed to perform the service, support re-testing,
        keep quality records, resolve disputes, meet accounting/tax or legal obligations, or establish,
        exercise or defend legal claims. After that period we delete, anonymise or destroy it under the
        sample policy. Sample-retention periods for a specific project are set by the order, service
        policy or written agreement.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">7. Cross-border processing</h2>
      <p>
        We are located in China and serve international clients. Cloud hosting, email, payment,
        logistics or laboratory providers may process information in other countries. Where required by
        law, we use contractual, consent-based or other lawful transfer mechanisms; the specific
        arrangement depends on the provider and project.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Subject to applicable law, you may request access to, a copy of, correction of or deletion of
        your personal information, withdraw consent, or object to or restrict certain processing. Use
        the <a href="/en/contact">contact page</a> and provide enough information for us to verify your
        identity. We respond within the period required by law; a request may be limited where retention
        is legally required, another person's rights are affected, or identity cannot be verified.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">9. Security and incidents</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable technical and organisational measures, including access controls, encryption
        in transit, least-privilege access and confidentiality requirements. No system is completely
        secure. If an incident may affect your rights, we will assess and handle it and provide notice
        where required by law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">10. Minors</h2>
      <p>
        The site and testing services are intended for clients with legal capacity, not for children. We
        do not knowingly collect children's personal information. If you believe a child has provided
        information, contact us so we can address it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">11. Cookies and policy changes</h2>
      <p>
        The site currently sets no analytics, advertising or tracking cookies; see the
        <a href="/en/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>. We may update this policy and publish the new version
        here; material changes will be highlighted where reasonable. Continued use of the site or
        services indicates awareness of the updated policy.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">12. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions, data requests or complaints: <a href="/en/contact">contact page</a> or
        <a href="mailto:martin@senobiocorp.com">martin@senobiocorp.com</a>. Related pages:
        <a href="/en/terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a>,
        <a href="/en/service-policy">Testing Service Policy</a>,
        <a href="/en/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>,
        <a href="/en/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
